WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.267 --> 00:00:02.968
-Rupert, welcome.
-Thank you for having me.

00:00:02.968 --> 00:00:04.801
-Well, I'm so happy you're here,

00:00:04.801 --> 00:00:06.634
because I want to get into
a bunch of things.

00:00:06.634 --> 00:00:10.901
But I know that when you joined
Instagram, it was a big deal.

00:00:10.901 --> 00:00:12.734
You broke the
Guinness World Record

00:00:12.734 --> 00:00:15.968
for the fastest person
to reach 1 million followers.

00:00:15.968 --> 00:00:18.100
[ Cheers and applause ]
-True. That's true.

00:00:18.100 --> 00:00:19.367
I know.

00:00:19.367 --> 00:00:23.033
-Now, here is actually
the first post right here.

00:00:23.033 --> 00:00:24.567
It says, "Hey, Instagram.

00:00:24.567 --> 00:00:26.567
Only 10 years late,
but here I am.

00:00:26.567 --> 00:00:27.868
Grint on the Gram.

00:00:27.868 --> 00:00:30.167
Here to introduce you all
to Wednesday G. Grint.

00:00:30.167 --> 00:00:31.901
Stay safe. Rupert."

00:00:31.901 --> 00:00:33.868
I mean, how beautiful is that?
Come on, you got --

00:00:33.868 --> 00:00:37.100
-Yeah. No, it was -- I mean,
I resisted joining

00:00:37.100 --> 00:00:38.100
Instagram for a long time.

00:00:38.100 --> 00:00:39.701
-Why?
-Just because I just --

00:00:39.701 --> 00:00:43.100
Ultimately, I think it just
doesn't go with my personality.

00:00:43.100 --> 00:00:44.334
-No.

00:00:44.334 --> 00:00:46.634
-I'm quite a shy person,
and the thought of kind of

00:00:46.634 --> 00:00:49.167
sharing my life just didn't seem
like it would really --

00:00:49.167 --> 00:00:51.434
-Yeah.
Are you good on Instagram?

00:00:51.434 --> 00:00:55.367
-No, I'm terrible.
Just -- It's really hard.

00:00:55.367 --> 00:00:57.434
Like, I never know what to post.

00:00:57.434 --> 00:00:58.968
-Well, I looked at
your Instagram

00:00:58.968 --> 00:01:00.400
to see what other things
we could show.

00:01:00.400 --> 00:01:04.267
You've only posted like
three other times since that.

00:01:04.267 --> 00:01:05.734
So you just kind of
just stopped and you go,

00:01:05.734 --> 00:01:06.801
"That's not my deal."

00:01:06.801 --> 00:01:09.801
-Yeah, it's mainly
"Servant" trailers

00:01:09.801 --> 00:01:12.467
and the back of my
daughter's head.

00:01:12.467 --> 00:01:15.267
-Yeah.
How is your baby daughter?

00:01:15.267 --> 00:01:16.501
-She's great.
-Oh, congratulations.

00:01:16.501 --> 00:01:17.701
How old?
-Thank you.

00:01:17.701 --> 00:01:19.734
Yeah, she's nearly 2.
She's like 21 months.

00:01:19.734 --> 00:01:21.601
-Oh, my gosh.
-It's great.

00:01:21.601 --> 00:01:23.968
-Oh, and great name, by the way.
Wednesday?

00:01:23.968 --> 00:01:25.300
-It's a good name, isn't it?
-Yes, I love Wednesday.

00:01:25.300 --> 00:01:27.701
-It's a strong name. Yeah.
-Why Wednesday?

00:01:27.701 --> 00:01:30.267
-Well, I mean,
I'm always hesitant to say

00:01:30.267 --> 00:01:33.234
it was "The Addams Family,"
but, it was, yeah,

00:01:33.234 --> 00:01:35.133
kind of "The Addams Family."

00:01:35.934 --> 00:01:37.234
I just always loved the name.

00:01:37.234 --> 00:01:38.467
-It's a cool --
It's a great name.

00:01:38.467 --> 00:01:40.000
-It's a good name.
It's kind of -- It's punchy.

00:01:40.000 --> 00:01:42.334
-Wednesday G. Grint.
-It's kind of memorable.

00:01:42.334 --> 00:01:44.033
-And the "G" -- what is that?

00:01:44.033 --> 00:01:45.667
-Yeah, so, actually,
Samuel L. Jackson

00:01:45.667 --> 00:01:46.667
kind of inspired that.

00:01:46.667 --> 00:01:47.834
-For real?

00:01:47.834 --> 00:01:49.901
-Yeah, we loved the idea of,
like, an initial,

00:01:49.901 --> 00:01:52.033
like Samuel L. Jackson,
Michael J. Fox,

00:01:52.033 --> 00:01:54.100
that kind of
speaking the initial.

00:01:54.100 --> 00:01:56.667
So she's Wednesday G. Grint.

00:01:56.667 --> 00:01:57.834
-Yes, I love that.

00:01:57.834 --> 00:01:59.300
-Yeah.
-That's fantastic.

00:01:59.300 --> 00:02:01.467
And fatherhood so far,
you loving it?

00:02:01.467 --> 00:02:02.534
-Loving it, yeah.
It's brilliant.

00:02:02.534 --> 00:02:04.501
Now she's kind of
talking and doing things,

00:02:04.501 --> 00:02:08.234
'cause for so long,
babies just don't do anything.

00:02:08.234 --> 00:02:10.934
-No, they actually
don't do anything, yeah.

00:02:10.934 --> 00:02:12.400
But now she's actually speaking?

00:02:12.400 --> 00:02:15.667
-She's speaking. She's talking.
She's got opinions.

00:02:15.667 --> 00:02:16.934
-She has opinions.

00:02:16.934 --> 00:02:19.434
Did she say
"dada" or "mama" first?

00:02:19.434 --> 00:02:21.434
-She says "dada."
She says "mama."

00:02:21.434 --> 00:02:23.133
It was kind at the same time.

00:02:23.133 --> 00:02:26.601
And, also, the F-word
came pretty quick.

00:02:26.601 --> 00:02:28.167
-Your baby says the F-word?
-She does.

00:02:28.167 --> 00:02:29.901
But she spends a lot of time
outside my dressing room

00:02:29.901 --> 00:02:31.100
when I'm kind of doing
my lines for this,

00:02:31.100 --> 00:02:35.234
and my character says
the F-word a lot.

00:02:35.234 --> 00:02:38.234
And now she just says
it whenever she's excited.

00:02:38.234 --> 00:02:42.234
We took her to -- Actually,
we were in a toy store today,

00:02:42.234 --> 00:02:45.067
and she was just walking around
just jumping at every --

00:02:45.067 --> 00:02:46.267
-And do people laugh
or what do people do?

00:02:46.267 --> 00:02:48.567
-Yeah, it's kind of
a mixed reaction.

00:02:48.567 --> 00:02:50.300
We find it hilarious,
so it's kind of encouraging it,

00:02:50.300 --> 00:02:51.300
but --

00:02:51.300 --> 00:02:53.434
-How big is -- She's tiny.

00:02:53.434 --> 00:02:55.100
-She's small.
Yeah, she's really small.

00:02:55.100 --> 00:02:57.934
-And says that.
-Yeah. Like I said --

00:02:57.934 --> 00:02:59.300
-Wednesday, watch it, watch it.

00:02:59.300 --> 00:03:02.000
You'll watch this clip one day
and -- Yeah.

00:03:02.000 --> 00:03:03.300
It's hard to believe,
but you celebrated --

00:03:03.300 --> 00:03:06.234
Is it 20th anniversary
of the first "Harry Potter"?

00:03:06.234 --> 00:03:08.367
-20 years, yeah.
-20 years ago. And --

00:03:08.367 --> 00:03:10.033
-Thank you. I know.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:10.033 --> 00:03:11.901
-You were a baby.
-Yeah.

00:03:11.901 --> 00:03:13.334
-You were a baby.

00:03:13.334 --> 00:03:16.100
And you had the big reunion with
a special with your castmates.

00:03:16.100 --> 00:03:17.701
Did you get along like,
"Oh, yeah,

00:03:17.701 --> 00:03:18.701
it's just like,
yeah, nothing, like --"

00:03:18.701 --> 00:03:19.834
It's just like riding a bike?

00:03:19.834 --> 00:03:21.100
You're like, "Yeah,
we know how to do this."

00:03:21.100 --> 00:03:23.367
-Yeah, it was kind of -- We just
kind of clicked straight

00:03:23.367 --> 00:03:24.834
back into --
I mean, it's been a long time.

00:03:24.834 --> 00:03:26.934
It's been 10 years since we
wrapped the last movie,

00:03:26.934 --> 00:03:28.968
and, yeah, time has past.

00:03:28.968 --> 00:03:31.901
I do feel like an old man now.

00:03:31.901 --> 00:03:34.067
-But you grew up --
I mean, you grew up on

00:03:34.067 --> 00:03:35.868
the sets with those --

00:03:35.868 --> 00:03:36.934
-Yeah, well, that's the thing.

00:03:36.934 --> 00:03:38.667
It's kind of more than
just eight films.

00:03:38.667 --> 00:03:40.234
It's like it was our childhood.

00:03:40.234 --> 00:03:42.367
-Yeah. Now you have a baby,
a beautiful baby,

00:03:42.367 --> 00:03:44.467
and you're going to show her
these movies one day

00:03:44.467 --> 00:03:45.467
and go, "That's dad."

00:03:45.467 --> 00:03:46.601
-Yeah, yeah, I know.

00:03:46.601 --> 00:03:47.601
I mean, I've already started
showing her

00:03:47.601 --> 00:03:50.100
the trailers, and she has a wand

00:03:50.100 --> 00:03:52.534
and a PEZ dispenser
with my head on it.

00:03:52.534 --> 00:03:54.667
-She has a PEZ dispenser
with your head on it?

00:03:54.667 --> 00:03:56.901
-We don't feed her PEZ,
but she has --

00:03:56.901 --> 00:03:58.968
-So every time you pull
daddy's head back,

00:03:58.968 --> 00:04:00.267
candy comes out of his neck?

00:04:00.267 --> 00:04:01.834
-Out of my throat, yeah.
-That's frightening, yeah.

00:04:01.834 --> 00:04:03.033
-It's kind of disturbing.

00:04:03.033 --> 00:04:05.234
-You can't do that --
-She's going with it.

00:04:05.234 --> 00:04:07.067
-Well, let's talk about
"Servant," because this is --

00:04:07.067 --> 00:04:09.267
It's the third season,
renewed for a fourth season.

00:04:09.267 --> 00:04:11.133
Congratulations on that.
-Thank you, yeah.

00:04:11.133 --> 00:04:16.133
M. Night Shyamalan is
brilliant -- beyond brilliant.

00:04:16.133 --> 00:04:17.901
I love that guy.
-Yeah.

00:04:17.901 --> 00:04:19.734
-You do a great American accent,
by the way.

00:04:19.734 --> 00:04:22.100
-Yeah, so, yeah, sort of --
-Oh, yeah, it's alright.

00:04:22.100 --> 00:04:24.033
Yeah, I can't do
British accents.

00:04:24.033 --> 00:04:25.901
[ British accent ]
I can't do that, you know?

00:04:25.901 --> 00:04:27.167
-Oh, that's quite good.
-Yeah, it's alright?

00:04:27.167 --> 00:04:28.167
-Yeah, that's alright.
I'll buy that.

00:04:28.167 --> 00:04:29.434
-So it's alright.
Yeah, of course.

00:04:29.434 --> 00:04:30.701
[ Normal voice ]
But that's all I can say.

00:04:30.701 --> 00:04:32.000
Is there a word
that's really hard to say

00:04:32.000 --> 00:04:33.300
in an American accent?

00:04:33.300 --> 00:04:36.234
-Yeah, I mean, there's a few
that kind of trip you up.

00:04:36.234 --> 00:04:39.734
One that stands out for me
was "floorboards."

00:04:39.734 --> 00:04:41.968
-Floorboards.
-[ American accent ] Floorboard.

00:04:41.968 --> 00:04:44.234
[ Normal voice ] Yeah,
it's like a -- I just --

00:04:44.234 --> 00:04:46.567
-You almost had
a Scottish or Irish.

00:04:46.567 --> 00:04:48.100
-Yeah, yeah.
-[ Scottish accent ] Floorboard.

00:04:48.100 --> 00:04:51.567
-Yeah. Yeah.
I just add like seven R's.

00:04:51.567 --> 00:04:53.767
-R's, yeah.
-But I think -- I don't know.

00:04:53.767 --> 00:04:56.901
It's lucky that it's not a word
that comes up very often.

00:04:56.901 --> 00:04:58.167
-Yeah, that's true.
It's not in many scripts.

00:04:58.167 --> 00:05:00.634
It's like, "can I change
the word 'floorboard' here?

00:05:00.634 --> 00:05:02.000
Is this a problem for anybody?"

00:05:02.000 --> 00:05:05.000
Yeah. Can you tell everyone, on
"Servant," who you play?

00:05:05.000 --> 00:05:06.234
-Sure, yeah.

00:05:06.234 --> 00:05:09.934
So -- Oh, man, I'm so bad
at explaining the show.

00:05:09.934 --> 00:05:11.434
-You can kind of --
I'll help you out.

00:05:11.434 --> 00:05:14.300
-Okay, yeah.
So, yeah, I play Julian.

00:05:14.300 --> 00:05:18.734
I'm Dorothy's brother.
Dorothy's just lost a baby.

00:05:18.734 --> 00:05:22.000
We meet her six months later,
and she's going through this

00:05:22.000 --> 00:05:24.234
radical therapy
where she uses a doll

00:05:24.234 --> 00:05:26.534
to kind of replace
the loss of her son.

00:05:26.534 --> 00:05:28.434
-But in the show,
you also get a nanny.

00:05:28.434 --> 00:05:30.234
-We get a nanny
to look after the doll.

00:05:30.234 --> 00:05:31.501
-The doll.
-Yeah.

00:05:31.501 --> 00:05:33.133
It kind of spirals out of
control, and --

00:05:33.133 --> 00:05:35.934
-It's M. Night, so it's, like --
You want those types of things

00:05:35.934 --> 00:05:37.367
to happen,
so it's all trippy and --

00:05:37.367 --> 00:05:38.734
-Yeah, yeah, it's very trippy.

00:05:38.734 --> 00:05:40.267
It kind of treads the line --
You never really know

00:05:40.267 --> 00:05:42.501
if there's kind of a
supernatural element going on.

00:05:42.501 --> 00:05:44.234
-Yeah.
-Yeah, it's a really fun show.

00:05:44.234 --> 00:05:46.067
-It's well done.
I want to show everyone a clip.

00:05:46.067 --> 00:05:48.701
Here's Rupert Grint
in the new season of "Servant."

00:05:48.701 --> 00:05:49.934
Take a look.

00:05:49.934 --> 00:05:51.534
-Uh, it's crooked.

00:05:51.534 --> 00:05:54.067
Look, you asked for my help.

00:05:54.067 --> 00:05:56.067
-[ Sighs ]
I was worried about you.

00:05:56.067 --> 00:05:58.968
I hadn't seen you lurking
around, raiding our fridge.

00:05:58.968 --> 00:06:01.534
-Five years of experience
of avoiding Dorothy's wrath.

00:06:01.534 --> 00:06:03.200
-You think she'll like it?

00:06:03.200 --> 00:06:04.534
-Yeah, she always did.

00:06:04.534 --> 00:06:07.434
It's supposed to be about
oppressed vaginas.

00:06:08.501 --> 00:06:10.601
I just see a black hole.

00:06:10.601 --> 00:06:14.000
Or are you asking me if it'll
make Dorothy like you again?

00:06:14.000 --> 00:06:16.100
-I'm doing every [bleep]
I can think of.

00:06:16.100 --> 00:06:18.934
I'm going to fix [bleep]
in the entry.

00:06:18.934 --> 00:06:20.434
Will you grab the tool bag?
-Yeah, you go ahead.

00:06:20.434 --> 00:06:22.834
I'll, uh, catch up.

00:06:22.834 --> 00:06:24.501
-Yeah, Rupert Grint, everybody.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:06:24.501 --> 00:06:28.634
New episodes of "Servant"
are available now on Apple TV+.

